<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<!-- H1-2 humanoid with Inspire RH56DFTP five-finger hands, flat URDF.

     GENERATED FILE, do not edit by hand. Regenerate after any change to the
     xacro sources with:

       xacro urdf/h1_2_with_inspire_hands.urdf.xacro -o urdf/h1_2_with_RH56DFTP_hands.urdf

     then restore this comment block and the robot name, which that command
     does not set.

     57 joints: 51 revolute and 6 fixed. Of the revolute ones, 27 are the body
     and 24 the hands, and 12 of those 24 are mimic, so the hands add 12
     independent DOF and the robot has 39 in total.

     Loading it in Pinocchio:

       import pinocchio as pin
       model = pin.buildModelFromUrdf(path, pin.JointModelFreeFlyer(), mimic=True)
       data  = model.createData()
       # nq = 46, nv = 45, total mass = 68.664 kg

     Pass mimic=True or the 12 coupled phalanges become independent joints and
     nv rises from 39 to 51. Pass JointModelFreeFlyer or the pelvis is welded to
     the universe body and computeTotalMass leaves out its 5.983 kg, reporting
     62.681 kg instead of 68.664 kg.

     Meshes are referenced as package://h1_2_inspire_description/meshes/...
     For geometry, give Pinocchio the package root:

       geom = pin.buildGeomFromUrdf(model, path, pin.GeometryType.VISUAL,
                                    package_dirs=["/path/to/your_ws/src"])
-->
<robot name="h1_2_with_RH56DFTP_hands">
